  "details": "1. Create an U# script that loads a URL, like the one below. Crucially, do not provide a receiver.\n\n2. Trigger it in-game (not in editor) and see the wrong error\n\n```\n\npublic class StringLoadTest : UdonSharpBehaviour\n\n{\n\n    public VRCUrl url;\n\n    [PublicAPI]\n\n    public void _Trigger()\n\n    {\n\n        VRCStringDownloader.LoadUrl(url);\n\n    }\n\n}\n\n```\n\nIf set to localhost or 127.0.0.1 in build & test, you will get the error saying it is not on the allowed video player URLs list for the world - despite not being an uploaded world.\n\nSetting the second parameter to `(IUdonEventReceiver)this` correctly fixes this error. This error does not show in unity play mode, this is an in-game issue.\n\nThis was tested both on the latest open beta as well as stable.",
